---
import { DiaTextReveal } from '../sora-ui/texts/dia-text-reveal';
import { SoraCtaButton } from '../sora-ui/SoraCtaButton';

const revealColors = ['#4d7cff', '#38bdf8', '#a5b4fc', '#e1e1fe'];
---

<section class="hero-section" id="mission">
  <div class="content-column">
    <div class="hero-header-super">
      <h1 class="hero-title">
        Recursive, self-improving infrastructure for{' '}
        <DiaTextReveal
          client:load
          className="hero-dia-reveal"
          text={[
            'scientific research.',
            'autonomous labs.',
            'discovery at scale.',
          ]}
          colors={revealColors}
          duration={1.4}
          holdDuration={2.2}
          repeat
          fixedWidth
        />
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        AI systems are already producing research-level advances in mathematics,
        with new AI-assisted discoveries appearing in rapid succession.
        Mathematics benefits from comparatively fast, abundant, and trustworthy
        verification. We are building that same loop for the rest of science.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-banner-container tick-box">
      <img
        src="/images/kalaris-hero-banner.png"
        alt="Kalaris Labs: Self-improving research infrastructure"
        width="1024"
        height="173"
        class="hero-banner-image"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="manifesto-stream">
      <p>
        The path to accelerated scientific discovery is to scale{' '}
        <a href="/manifesto" class="source-backlink">
          in-context recursive learning<span
            class="backlink-icon"
            aria-hidden="true">↗</span
          >
        </a>{' '}
        that works with any model, any experimental harness, and across all research
        disciplines. As scientific models proliferate and the frontier becomes multi-domain,
        experimental context and operational tooling should be separated from fragile
        one-off scripts and compound continuously.
      </p>

      <p class="manifesto-callout">
        <a href="/manifesto" class="source-backlink callout-link">
          <DiaTextReveal
            client:visible
            text="Operational overhead is no longer a constraint."
            colors={revealColors}
            duration={1.6}
          /><span class="backlink-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </p>

      <p>
        Pre-training and post-training, scaling on data and compute, will
        continue to push foundational models' capabilities, but will not enable
        them to learn, adapt, and improve experiments in real time.
      </p>

      <p>
        We build all the hard infrastructure parts of a scalable research
        engine, with{' '}
        <a href="/blog/closed-loop-science" class="source-backlink">
          dense, interconnected, compounding learnings<span
            class="backlink-icon"
            aria-hidden="true">↗</span
          >
        </a>, and an understanding of scientific lineage.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our architecture helps research teams continuously improve by extracting
        and synthesizing context from papers, codebases, and experimental
        iterations: injecting verified context into autonomous agents in real
        time.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-actions">
        <SoraCtaButton client:load href="/manifesto">
          Read the manifesto →
        </SoraCtaButton>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/research">
          Explore research <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
